  "explanation": "Exercise 2.2 applies all laws of integral exponents: product law (add exponents), quotient law (subtract), power of a power (multiply exponents), negative exponents (reciprocal), and finding unknown exponents by equating bases. When bases match on both sides, compare exponents directly.",
